BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salvation
DTSTART:20260512T201500Z
DTEND:20260512T222500Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T201500Z
UID:wYT4dis1gw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nIn a historical moment when an 
 “us versus them” mentality is fueling polarization around the world\, 
 director Emin Alper grapples with this issue in a timeless tale with real-
 world resonance.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/salvation\n\nEstimated s
 tart: 13:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hen
DTSTART:20260512T230000Z
DTEND:20260513T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T230000Z
UID:KWD5Sk2uSG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nA runaway hen finds refuge in a c
 rumbling Greek taverna and bears witness to a human-smuggling operation. H
 en proves motherhood looks the same across species. If you think this is a
  goofy movie about a chicken\, you couldn’t be more wrong.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/festival/hen\n\nEstimated start: 16:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RADIOHEART: The Drive and Times of DJ Kevin Cole
DTSTART:20260513T013000Z
DTEND:20260513T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T013000Z
UID:JQ9wOnSGsO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 83 mins (1h23m)\n\nIn his 25-year tenure at KEXP\, D
 J Kevin Cole helped define not just who Seattle listens to\, but how we li
 sten\, fostering delight and curiosity with every recommendation. RADIOHEA
 RT\, a bio-doc about Cole’s remarkable life\, boasts a killer soundtrack
 \, a wealth of nostalgic archival footage\, and cameos from Seattle musica
 l legends.Directors Peter Hilgendorf and Andrew Franks\, plus Producer Reb
 ecca Staffel and Subject Kevin Cole scheduled to attend.This film is gener
 ously sponsored by David Prokopy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/radiohe
 art-the-drive-and-times-of-dj-kevin-cole\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown
  House 1 (Fri 15 May\, 3:30 PM)\n  • Uptown House 1 (Sun 17 May\, 8:00 P
 M)\n\nEstimated start: 18:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renoir
DTSTART:20260513T040000Z
DTEND:20260513T061000Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T040000Z
UID:arsjC3rpdG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nA coming-of-age story following 
 a tomboyish 11-year-old girl whose intellectual father is dying of cancer 
 and mother at her wits’ end. The courageous girl seeks adventures\, some
  involving the paranormal.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/renoir\n\nEsti
 mated start: 21:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beat the Lotto
DTSTART:20260513T194500Z
DTEND:20260513T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T194500Z
UID:EU7amx5YJW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nWhen Ireland inaugurated its Nati
 onal Lottery\, it became a national obsession. One man soon discovered a f
 law in the system\, gaming the odds to win it all and dividing the nation 
 in the process.Director Ross Whitaker scheduled to attend May 17 screening
 .\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/beat-the-lotto\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • PACCAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center (Sun 17 May\, 4:00 PM)\n
 \nEstimated start: 12:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maspalomas
DTSTART:20260513T220000Z
DTEND:20260514T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T220000Z
UID:HeImw5ccUL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 115 mins (1h55m)\n\nAfter a stroke while vacationing
  in the gay haven of Maspalomas\, Vicente—played by José Ramón Soroiz\
 , winner of the 2026 Goya Award for Best Lead Actor—is placed in a nursi
 ng home where he’s forced back into the closet\, confronting a fight for
  freedom he thought he’d already won.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/m
 aspalomas\n\nEstimated start: 15:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Visions
DTSTART:20260514T010000Z
DTEND:20260514T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T010000Z
UID:b23c4XqNkZ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nA cast of quirky characters\, in
 cluding an animatronic cowboy and a marathoner with a soft spot for Dick
 ’s burgers\, star in these Washington-made shorts that showcase the vita
 lity of our local filmmaking community. Filmmakers scheduled to attend. S
 tudy your local film trivia before attending the screening because the Sea
 ttle Film Society will be giving away tickets to one of their upcoming ev
 ents! After the screening\, join them and Seattle Documentary Association
  for their Spring Mixer at Queen Anne Beer Hall.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /festival/sound-visions-x41556\n\nEstimated start: 18:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Promised Sky
DTSTART:20260514T041500Z
DTEND:20260514T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T041500Z
UID:bS08RaJ5Bf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nA community of Ivorian women navi
 gating the complexities of migrant life in Tunisia are forced to make diff
 icult decisions when they rescue an orphaned girl from a shipwreck.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/promised-sky\n\nEstimated start: 21:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hijra
DTSTART:20260514T193000Z
DTEND:20260514T213500Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T193000Z
UID:K16D0MybVR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 114 mins (1h54m)\n\nSitti is on a pilgrimage to Mecc
 a with her two rebellious granddaughters\, Sarah and Janna. But everything
  changes when one of the granddaughters goes missing.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/festival/hijra\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 2 (Wed 13 May\,
  9:00 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 12:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When a Witness Recants
DTSTART:20260514T220000Z
DTEND:20260515T001000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T220000Z
UID:IajkjyWMwu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 117 mins (1h57m)\n\nThe story of the three Black Bal
 timore teens wrongfully incarcerated in 1983 for the murder of a classmate
 \, exonerated 36 years later\, delving into the prosecutorial and police m
 isconduct\, and the collateral damage on the wrongfully accused and the wh
 ole community.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/when-a-witness-recants\n\n
 Estimated start: 15:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life We Leave
DTSTART:20260515T010000Z
DTEND:20260515T024000Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T010000Z
UID:N56IhfPRM1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 87 mins (1h27m)\n\nAn ambitious entrepreneur and two
  funeral directors pioneer a groundbreaking eco-friendly deathcare facilit
 y in Washington state\, challenging traditional burial practices and trans
 forming end-of-life rituals.Recipient of a 2024 SIFF Grant for Courageous 
 Documentary Filmmaking. The 2026 Grant Cycle opens May 15 on the SIFF webs
 ite. Director JJ Gerber and subjects Micah Truman\, Brie Smith\, and Katey
  Houston scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-life-we
 -leave\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 2 (Sat 16 May\, 1:00 PM)\n\
 nEstimated start: 18:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silent Friend
DTSTART:20260515T033000Z
DTEND:20260515T061000Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T033000Z
UID:JorO9Zm7Oj
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 146 mins (2h26m)\n\nAward-winning director Ildikó E
 nyedi delivers another mesmerizing visual tale\, set across three time per
 iods at a historic German university\, united by a gingko tree. This film 
 is generously sponsored by Dale Pratt.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/si
 lent-friend\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Tue 12 May\, 2:30 PM)\n\n
 Estimated start: 20:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hanging by a Wire
DTSTART:20260515T200000Z
DTEND:20260515T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T200000Z
UID:cOsfvjxrP9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 77 mins (1h17m)\n\nIn remote northern Pakistan\, sch
 oolchildren cross a canyon by cable car each day—until one morning\, two
  of the three cables snap\, turning their routine journey into a desperate
  fight for survival as they are suspended 900 feet in the air.Director Mo
 hammed Ali Naqvi and Producer Bilal Sami scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://w
 ww.siff.net/festival/hanging-by-a-wire\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • PACCAR I
 MAX Theater at Pacific Science Center (Thu 14 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\nEstimated 
 start: 13:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
