BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Primavera
DTSTART:20260516T010000Z
DTEND:20260516T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T010000Z
UID:tHpFH88TZ9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nInspired by Antonio Vivaldi’s 
 nearly three decades at the Ospedale della Pietà\, where orphaned girls p
 erformed from behind screens and convent walls\, this dramatic story follo
 ws Cecilia—a gifted young virtuoso who refused to be silenced.  This fi
 lm is generously sponsored by Peggy & Dennis Willingham.\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/primavera\n\nEstimated start: 18:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maddie's Secret
DTSTART:20260516T033000Z
DTEND:20260516T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T033000Z
UID:DA292ZuD3i
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nUnmissable directorial debut sat
 irizing and skewering content culture from iconic alt-comedian John Early\
 , who plays the titular role\, alongside a troupe of comedians including K
 ate Berlant\, Vanessa Bayer\, and Conner O’Malley.\n\nhttps://www.siff.n
 et/festival/maddies-secret\n\nEstimated start: 20:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Another World
DTSTART:20260516T190000Z
DTEND:20260516T210500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T190000Z
UID:p1gXNvpDbR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 111 mins (1h51m)\n\nA harrowing\, arrestingly render
 ed epic of revenge and redemption that announces director Tommy Kai Chung 
 Ng as a massive new voice in the world of animation. Local artists Zine H
 ug will be selling prints in the lobby before both showtimes.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/festival/another-world\n\nEstimated start: 12:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Want Your Sex
DTSTART:20260516T214500Z
DTEND:20260516T232500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T214500Z
UID:Afxqc0dk6E
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nWhen fresh-faced Elliot (Cooper H
 offman) lands an exciting job for renowned artist\, icon\, and provocateur
  Erika Tracy (Olivia Wilde)\, his fantasies come true as Erika taps him to
  become her sexual muse.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i-want-your-sex\
 n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Fri 15 May\, 9:15 PM)\n\nEstimated st
 art: 14:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Phoenix Jones: The Rise and Fall of a Real Life Superhero
DTSTART:20260517T003000Z
DTEND:20260517T024000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T003000Z
UID:1A08Inl2WO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nReal-life superhero\, or untrain
 ed vigilante? A new documentary revisits the Phoenix Jones saga\, a fascin
 ating chapter in recent Seattle history\, with never-before-seen footage a
 nd illuminating interviews with Phoenix’s family\, co-superheroes\, and 
 enemies. Director Bayan Joonam and Producer Claire Chubbuck scheduled to a
 ttend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/phoenix-jones-the-rise-and-fall-of
 -a-real-life-superhero\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 1 (Sun 17 M
 ay\, 2:00 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 17:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Three Goodbyes
DTSTART:20260517T033000Z
DTEND:20260517T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T033000Z
UID:E49s5nUCJW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 124 mins (2h04m)\n\nAfter years together\, Marta and
  Antonio are undone by an argument that should have amounted to nothing. W
 hen Marta’s loss of appetite turns out to be about more than heartbreak\
 , everything she thought she knew about her life comes into question.\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/festival/three-goodbyes\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • PAC
 CAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center (Tue 12 May\, 5:45 PM)\n\nEstim
 ated start: 20:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lady
DTSTART:20260517T183000Z
DTEND:20260517T201500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T183000Z
UID:k5MH3V8ik0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nIn this absurdly hilarious mockum
 entary\, a young filmmaker agrees to film the behind-the-scenes vanity pro
 ject of the obnoxiously entitled Lady Isabella\, only for something unseen
  and quite strange to happen.Director Samuel Abrahams scheduled to attend 
 the May 16 screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/lady\n\nAlso playin
 g at:\n  • Uptown House 2 (Sat 16 May\, 3:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 11:
 40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
